Description: the patches of the FreeBSD port security/libssh2 (its PATCHFILES, three upstream commits): CMake fixes (unused by this build, configure) and the bounds check of the user name length in userauth.c (#1858); CVE-2026-55200 (transport.c), CVE-2026-55199 (packet.c) and CVE-2025-15661 (sftp.c), which the port lacks; and CVE-2026-66032 (a double free in sftp_open(), sftp.c), CVE-2026-66033 (an integer underflow with AES-GCM in the cipher of openssl.c, before the authentication), CVE-2026-66034, CVE-2026-58050 and CVE-2026-58051 (an out-of-bounds read, a multiplication overflow on 32-bit and an arbitrary free in libssh2_publickey_list_fetch(), publickey.c) and CVE-2026-66035 (a heap overflow on the ETM decryption of a short packet, transport.c, before the authentication): from a malicious SSH server to the client (curl SFTP and SCP, PHP ssh2, mc); and the fixes of libssh2 master after them (no release yet): a server whose list of key exchange methods matches only the pseudo methods ext-info-c or kex-strict-c-v00@openssh.com made the client take one of them and call its exchange_keys, which is NULL (a crash before the login; such a method is never taken now, and its exchange is an error: GHSA-92x4-f995-pjxq); libssh2_sftp_symlink() reported a failure for a link it had made, as the fix of CVE-2025-15661 read the request id as the status code (ssh2_sftp_symlink() of PHP, symlink of curl, mc), and a NAME reply to a SYMLINK request was copied into the name of the link the caller gave; libssh2_session_method_pref() accepted a list of key exchange methods it does not know (ssh2_connect() of PHP with a wrong kex: no error, a failing handshake later); a double free of the mkdir packet after a failed write; the packet length unchecked with the ETM MACs (GHSA-949f-w9qj-9q6h); an SFTP read in a loop on an end of the channel in the middle of a packet (GHSA-2q3j-q544-xxp7); a packet with no payload left after its padding read on. Ours: the MD5 MACs hmac-md5 and hmac-md5-96 behind LIBSSH2_NO_HMAC_MD5 (mac.c), so that the build can leave them out (curl/build-libcurl.sh, with LIBSSH2_NO_3DES, LIBSSH2_NO_RC4, LIBSSH2_NO_BLOWFISH and LIBSSH2_NO_CAST of 1.11.1: aZ, 12.11.2026) while keeping the MD5 of the host key fingerprint (libssh2_hostkey_hash(): ssh2_fingerprint() of PHP by default, --hostpubmd5 of curl) and of old PEM keys, which LIBSSH2_NO_MD5 takes away too
Origin: freebsd-ports security/libssh2 @ f16b6dd0f7c1 (PATCHFILES 5d03b4f94ac6, d4e43c7b69d1, 256d04b60d80 of https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2), -p0; Gentoo net-libs/libssh2 1.11.1-r2 (bug 977961): upstream 97acf3dfda80 (CVE-2026-55200), the result checks of _libssh2_get_string() in packet.c (CVE-2026-55199), upstream 2dae3024897e (CVE-2025-15661); CVE-2026-66032, -66033, -66034, -66035 (upstream 5e47761, a2ed82d, a13bb6c, 42e33d8) and CVE-2026-58050, -58051 (upstream 3449752, 32092f0) as Debian carries them on 1.11.1 (libssh2 1.11.1-5 and -6, https://sources.debian.org/src/libssh2/1.11.1-6/debian/patches/; Ubuntu 26.04 1.11.1-1ubuntu0.26.04.4, Alpine 1.11.1-r4 and openSUSE the same set), in this order after the ones above; upstream https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/631e2f82a32ef016299ebb1af66efeae0161f68e (#1763, 19.12.2025, as Homebrew carries it) with https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/22bba2ef5b0e189ad16db4c4e7da4a7c55683465 (GHSA-92x4-f995-pjxq, 06.11.2026), https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/4ed26f5740bdd409269ed9fb48a28bf8f565b681 (#1731, as OpenEmbedded carries it, CVE-2025-15661-3.patch, and Buildroot, 0006-sftp-symlink-fix-SSH_FXP_STATUS-response.patch) with https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/6125bfe552b3a8c7340c2fb3b82cdf65b0e16f9d (07.11.2026), https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/4beed7245889ba149cc372f845d5969ce5103a5d (#1554, as OpenEmbedded carries it, 0001-Return-error-if-user-KEX-methods-are-invalid.patch), https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/b9254798b6437af5dd43180c6d3b3db555f03f6e (02.11.2026), https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/70864b47b33ba330a6ba0fa5e7da9a9a6da8efb7 (GHSA-949f-w9qj-9q6h, 02.11.2026), https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/9438f90ae03f52d54297f15ef23b05ebb7c5f598 (GHSA-2q3j-q544-xxp7, 03.09.2026), https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/441ca6df7c8f1816c7ea477348c45645f1cc4102 (10.11.2026), those of master on the code of 1.11.1 (the names of its functions); the switch of the